WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.160
Having polluted the whole of Earth, mankind emigrated into space,

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.160
ushering in an era in which it became a familiar home for him.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:43.260
But, in space as on Earth, the human race repeated its history of war.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:51.160
Perhaps it was their instincts as they tried to adapt to a new environment...

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.330
...that caused their foolishness to return.

00:01:56.730 --> 00:02:02.360
If people can't bring themselves to believe that they can live in space,

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.860
mankind's history will be a tragic one.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.530
Once Üso returned from Uwig,

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.230
he became determined to fight in Kasarelia.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.160
I guess Miss Katejina Loos doesn't like babies.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.260
Look, Karl! You drank it all!

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.960
FOR WHOM DO WE FIGHT?

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.300
"For Whom Do We Fight?"
FOR WHOM DO WE FIGHT?

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.160
FOR WHOM DO WE FIGHT?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.760
Will everyone be staying here?

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:51.860
Is this alright?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.900
Looks like it!

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.760
You should spread it out on the other side, too.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.560
Roger!

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.800
That should do it.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.330
Oh, Üso...

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.300
Looks like the baby's named Karlmann Dukatus. See?

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:13.360
Karlmann?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.400
What's everyone doing?

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.400
We can't move till the core fighter's repaired, right?

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.260
So they said they're preparing for if the enemy comes.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.400
Okay! Take that to Üso!

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.200
Haro!

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.560
Warren, bring Odelo down now.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:31.260
Okay.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.660
Can we use this, too?

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.700
No. There's no way to mount it on the ground.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.160
Odelo, let's move!

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.100
Haro!

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.230
Thanks.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.700
You're putting up a barrier?

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.130
That's the plan.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.860
Right! I'll just ask the man in charge.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:57.460
Oh, Miss Shahkti. Thank you for sharing food with everyone.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.060
Oh, you're welcome.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.700
If we really try to fight here, everyone is going to die.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:18.100
According to Garry's map, they should be northwest of Uwig.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.530
Well, just get some rest, Garry.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:27.860
Since I took ground fire, I need to have a rematch.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.730
See how repentant Ensign Sabat is?

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.300
While you, Ltjg. Cronicle, left the Shokew...

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.130
It was stolen by enemies, as I reported.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:39.360
Without suffering any injury?

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.300
Correct.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:45.460
You can't ignore that Ensign Garry was seriously injured by that Shokew!

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.760
Since you were piloting the test suit, I imagine you want to steal it back.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.030
Of course, sir.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:56.200
Then, under Sabat's command, you should get your chance.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.730
Such experiences will be good for your future.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.630
Yes, sir. Thank you.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:03.530
Go!

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.230
We'll be off then, Dupré.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.100
It's for his education.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.030
Haro!

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.360
Üso, did you say you have some computer chips?

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.030
Not many kinds, though.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.860
Would you show us?

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.830
Sure.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:26.960
Climb on.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:27.700
Yes, sir.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:28.800
Go ahead.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.260
Maybe he'll calm down if you take him for a walk.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.230
Right.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.300
Are they headed for the mobile suit?

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:39.630
This should do it.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.860
Where are they going?

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.230
The chips are in those drawers.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.200
Let's have a look.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:46.760
These are...

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:47.960
Wow!

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:51.100
What are these doing here?

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.500
My dad collected them.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.230
You mean these old arcade machines?

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:54.930
Hardly.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.400
There's stuff here we could use for the core fighter.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.800
The real collection's underground.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.900
What are these cables on the ceiling?

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:04.000
They connect to the computer bank.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.930
Looks like there was an earthquake.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:06.700
Yeah.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.900
My parents lived here because it had all this.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.030
This is impressive.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.930
Most of it is government documents, but there's a library, too.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.800
And that's what you studied?

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.030
It's in here.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.630
That's an early mobile suit simulator, isn't it?

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.800
Look. Do you know what coastline this is?

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.100
The North American coast, maybe?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.730
Well, I'm starting to understand you a bit more.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:36.860
Well?

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:39.760
I think about five are usable. May I, Üso?

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:40.630
Sure.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.660
The terminal in his house is connected to this computer?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.100
It's all stuff from another era.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.130
But it's usable, isn't it?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.100
My dad taught me how to use them.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:54.500
And you studied the materials in here?

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:58.130
Yeah. The library has general education materials, too.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.460
I'm amazed that it still works. The data it must contain...

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:02.860
Oh, it lost power.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.760
That happens all the time.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.330
Hey, let's study here, too.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.860
What's the point?!

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.060
There, there...

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.160
Üso, you're leaving again?

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.130
Would you ride with me, Miss Katejina?

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.030
It's okay. I'd rather walk.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:22.360
Oh...

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:28.760
What's she doing?

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.660
Karlmann gets cranky if you don't walk him around.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:32.960
You won't get on?

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.660
It's okay. I'll walk.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:36.860
I see.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.530
We're here, Garry.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:47.730
I doubt the resistance will stay in one place for very long.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.730
Ltjg. Cronicle, what do you think?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.960
Calling Commander Sabat. The river ahead has to be it.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.960
Requesting permission to investigate.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:02.130
You're not likely to have any luck looking where there's already been a battle.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:06.700
Maybe if we were facing real soldiers, but the ones crawling around here are...

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:09.560
The word is that the League Militaire are real soldiers!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.800
We should torch the entire area!

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:16.360
But feel free to investigate till we do, Lieutenant.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.830
Otis, are we safe?

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.560
I hesitate to say we're safe, but...

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.130
Keep quiet!

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.360
Let's spring the trap!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.030
Don't be stupid! Like we'd pull off such a lucky shot?

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:37.600
There, there...

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.400
Good boy. Be a good boy.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.800
What's that wire? It doesn't look like a power line.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:06.530
Wait! You, girl! Stop!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.700
Flanders, stop.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.930
Miss, I have one question to ask.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:13.530
Yes?

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.360
What's that wire strung between the trees for?

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.800
Wire?

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.130
If you live around here, you must know.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.530
A... A telephone line. For us.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:28.860
Oh? You illegals don't use radios?

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.060
R-Right.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.700
Sabat, it's too soon!

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.530
Miss, take that wappa and run for the mountaintop!

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.860
If you sit here crying, you're gonna die! Get up, Suzy!

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:57.860
Can you drive?

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.630
I don't have much choice, do I?

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.330
Otis, we're moving to the Uwig area!

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.500
Don't worry, we'll catch up with you later!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.730
Odelo, hurry! They're about to hit this place, too!

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:10.530
Crying isn't going to keep the enemy away, you know!

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.160
Shahkti!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.360
Shahkti! Shahkti!

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:29.860
Haro! Haro! Haro!

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:31.660
Shahkti!

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.660
The forest is burning!

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:39.830
Yes, it might burn down, so follow the Camion and escape!

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.600
It's because of them this is happening!

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.060
Don't cry, Karlmann!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.160
This is no time to be arguing about that!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.000
This is your only choice right now!

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.160
They're over that way! Now get going!

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.060
Don't make this any harder for me.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:52.130
Right...

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.930
I'll help the Camion escape.

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:57.630
Flanders, Haro, protect Shahkti!

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:58.460
Haro!

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:00.600
But, Shahkti...

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:05.000
Don't get too close to the Camion. Just follow them, okay?

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:15.630
We can't let the Camion stay here. It can't be helped.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:29.130
Do they think there's something in the ruins?

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:57.430
Shahkti, you're too close to the Camion!

00:11:58.500 --> 00:11:59.960
Why are they stopped here?

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.600
Marbet, don't push yourself!

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:04.730
What are you planning?

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:08.330
I need to sortie the core fighter and draw the enemy away!

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.230
They're going to find everyone!

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.900
Yes, but can you do it with your injured leg?

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:13.800
I'll manage!

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.660
Üso! He's on the move!

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:18.400
In that conspicuous thing? He'll be spotted!

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:19.600
Üso is?

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.300
Üso? What's wrong?

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.160
Üso, stop!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:28.560
You've had a few lucky breaks, but you can't count on that!

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:31.860
Turn right, and it'll take you straight to the river.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:35.400
It might be a little tight, but head straight to the right!

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.800
Shahkti's right behind you, too! Please!

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:38.600
Thanks!

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.760
Got it, Üso? Don't push it too far.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.800
Are you going out, too, Miss Marbet?

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.130
Yeah, so please...

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:47.630
Miss Katejina...

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:55.900
Her face... She doesn't approve, but she's not afraid of me, either.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:56.960
Why?

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:58.500
Of course!

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:03.460
Üso took the rifle from the truck!

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:05.760
Üso, that thing is powerful!

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.130
Üso!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:22.960
They're close! Aren't there any weapons I can use to distract the enemy?

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.360
One of the leg machines!

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.200
This is as close as you're gonna get!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.100
I can't see it.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.660
I'm just wasting ammo. Where is he?!

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:48.300
To Commander Sabat and all units! The Shokew just flew out of the smoke!

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.530
Cronicle unit is now docking with the Boots!

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.960
This is Sabat. Shokew, confirmed!

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:02.160
Units 2 and 3, assist Cronicle! Dock in sequence.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:02.930
Roger! Roger!

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:08.530
I can't hit it!

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.730
If they get me into a hand-to-hand mobile suit battle,

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:12.300
I'll never beat their numbers!

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:13.960
Karbin, let's dock!

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.930
No! I won't let you dock!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:25.200
The Minovsky sensors are offline! Beam rotors, too!

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:31.230
It wasn't a direct hit?

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:34.230
No, wait. Hitting their engine directly would be bad.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:35.730
What should I do?

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.100
Sabat unit! Docking, complete!

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.500
Minovsky particles have been scattered.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:42.630
Unit 2! Jim!

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:45.160
Even if you don't hear from me, dock when you get the chance!

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:45.960
Roger!

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:46.930
There!

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:50.500
Young master Cronicle is too damn slow!

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.060
Unit 2, follow me! We'll surround him!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:02.360
It's no use.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.030
I can't hit anything because I can't hold the gun steady!

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.200
It's fast!

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:11.460
Cronicle! Jim! Don't you understand?! Surround it!

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.930
Are the Shokew's basic abilities improving?

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:15.460
We can't let it escape!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.060
That jet's taking off.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.400
Mr. Romero! Get the Hanger ready to send out, too!

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.930
I hear you! That's what I was planning!

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:32.060
You're just guiding her out to look cool, aren't you?!

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:38.130
What? I can't hear you over the Minovsky noise!

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:39.960
What is it, Leonid?!

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:42.300
She's going to dock them?

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.330
What's old man Romero up to?

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.360
He's launching the Hanger on the Camion in front of us.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.060
Odelo.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:57.900
Okay, then...

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:01.430
If we swing the crane out, it'll hit the trees!

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.700
Then raise it!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.130
Otis, do it!

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:05.130
Get ready!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.460
We can't leave Marbet hanging!

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:08.400
Right!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:14.600
They're crazy. These people are all crazy!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.300
G-Get the tarp off!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.460
Right!

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:22.760
Üso, maneuver more!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.930
I may not have a G-suit, but...

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:34.130
A mini-fighter! The one Garry mentioned!

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:35.500
Cronicle! Jim!

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:36.160
What?!

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.300
Just a fighter?

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:40.160
There it is! Because that thing showed up, I was...

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:46.600
Relying just on firepower won't let you win, Üso! Understand?

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:48.530
Who's that? Miss Marbet?

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.630
Its movements are improving.

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.430
Get away from her!

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.960
An empty test suit can't beat me!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:01.860
Out of ammo.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:04.460
This is for Garry!

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:15.060
You defeated my comrade, and even Cronicle couldn't beat you!

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:16.700
I'll finish you!

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:18.560
Odelo!

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:19.560
Gotcha!

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:23.530
We've got it all set. Come and get it, Miss Marbet!

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.000
What is that?

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:28.900
It improves the core fighter's firepower.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.530
Shahkti, get in the vehicle up ahead!

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:39.860
All we can do now is trust in Marbet's good luck.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:41.500
That's the kind of girl she is.

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:43.130
You really won't get in?

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.860
No. I'm sorry.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.230
Shahkti, why?!

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:51.100
I don't really want to leave Kasarelia.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.600
I'll be okay here on my own.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:00.230
In the end, it's just a little plane with no weapons.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.730
Unit 2, Jim! Let's squeeze it from the sides!

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:07.630
Count, where are you? I'm out of ammo!

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.560
Found it!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:16.860
If not for these Minovsky particles...

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.260
There?

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.030
What's that smoke?

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:40.700
If they attack me here, I'm finished.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.760
Please, God... move! Here they come!

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:45.860
What?!

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.530
Hanger, fly!

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:52.560
They were hiding a new model?

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.130
The beam gain is too different!

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.100
Sabat, they got Jim in Unit 2! Sabat!

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:17.500
We should have cornered them! How did they set a trap?!

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:21.830
That wire... This is where we set the trap.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:23.800
There's a rifle here.

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:28.230
I think the Shokew has something in its shoulder.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:34.700
Gotcha!

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:40.130
A trap! Where is it?!

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.300
In this case, rather than drag on this knife fight...

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.830
Sabat! I can't rely on his firepower and he can't support me.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:53.800
Where is he?!

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.260
The Shokew!

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:04.830
Sabat, was all that tough talk just bluster?

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:12.100
That little beam can't hit me! How do you like this?!

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.630
Trying to distract me! Shoulder beam!

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:27.630
Damn you!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:38.800
It didn't explode... It didn't explode, but...

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:42.260
What... What did I hear?

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:44.700
Üso... What are you doing?

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.660
Üso... Don't die.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:11.130
I'm still...

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:14.200
Help me, Mother!

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:20.430
Father... Mother...

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:28.100
The shoulder gun! Dammit!

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.230
The emergency...

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:48.530
Fighting in a mobile is terrifying. Üso understands that.

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:50.530
And yet...

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.430
Okay, Üso! Give it a try.

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:55.060
Yes, sir.

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.500
Otis, don't fall!

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:59.860
This mobile suit they call Victory...

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:01.660
Okay?

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:02.900
Slowly, now.

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:06.230
It may have possessed Üso.

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:31.730 --> 00:23:34.830
The people from the underground factory...

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:37.730
...have come to see Üso as Victory's pilot.

00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:42.660
And that will lead him into even more terrifying ordeals.

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:45.530
Among the Yellow Jackets, too,

00:23:45.560 --> 00:23:49.700
there is one who harbors a grudge and attacks the Victory.

00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:54.130
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:54.960
"Godzorla's Counterattack".

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:56.660
Next Episode GODZORLA'S COUNTERATTACK

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:57.930
Please watch it!
